<!--
  MachineBlocks — concept documentation

  FQN: com.machineblocks.bml.documentation.concept.DecisionFramework
-->
<block
  xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
  xsi:schemaLocation="http://blockml.org/bml https://blockml.org/schemas/bml.xsd
                      "
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:concept="com.machineblocks.bml.documentation.concept"
  xmlns:mbml="com.machineblocks.bml.documentation.mbml"
  xmlns:scad="com.machineblocks.bml.documentation.scad">

  <name>DecisionFramework</name>
  <type>concept:DecisionFramework</type>
  <baseType>core:Documentation</baseType>
  <is>A guide to MachineBlocks decision layers</is>

  <documentation>
    Do not start with parameters — start with intent. Three decision layers apply whether authoring
    in MBML or targeting SCAD:

    1. Semantic Intent — what is this block for?
    2. Pattern Selection — how is it structured?
    3. Parameter Realization — how is it built?

    Intent order: Semantic Mode (purpose, structure, printability) is primary. Output Mode chooses
    LEGO-like (playful, looser) versus Device (functional, strict printability). Design Mode
    (appearance) is secondary and never overrides purpose.

    Pattern selection: Primitive Wrapper, Semantic/Simple Block, Composite Block, or Helper/Form.
    When in doubt, choose Composite.

    Capability boundary of a single native geometry call: classic bricks and plates, slopes or
    wedges (not both in one call), rounds, recess, studs, simple cutouts, and similar single-body
    forms. L/T/cross shapes, Z-brackets, side panels, cable channels, bent liftarms, multi-line
    text, and multi-body carriers require composition.

    Cross-cutting rules: design in west-local face semantics; prefer direction over free rotation;
    keep calibration adjustments out of instance settings when they belong in config; use face
    string identifiers in V3.

    TODO — Decision Knowledge package: Long-term, grow this into a large structured collection
    (best practices, antipatterns/negative examples, pattern choices, boundaries, rules) under
    com.machineblocks.bml.decision.* — not under documentation.*. Own knowledge branch types
    (e.g. Practice, Antipattern, DecisionRule, PatternChoice) with typed relations to
    NativeBlock / CompositeBlock / examples. Migrate this block and scad:ScadDecisionRules into
    that package; keep documentation.concept|mbml|scad as reading guides that only cross-link in.
  </documentation>

  <references>
    <see type="concept:StatusConvention" relation="ReadNext">
      Next — status Block references for maturity.
    </see>
    <see type="mbml:AuthoringPatterns" relation="SeeAlso">
      MBML realization of these patterns.
    </see>
    <see type="scad:ScadDecisionRules" relation="SeeAlso">
      SCAD-specific decision rules and mb_block() whitelist/blacklist.
    </see>
  </references>

</block>
